# Posts: run top to bottom. Each login replaces the stored cookie.
# Passwords come from api/.env (requests/.env is a symlink to it).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:5174
@json = application/json

### 1. Public list: only published posts, no content, with excerpt -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts

### 2. Log in as author1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 3. Create a post: always starts as a draft -> 201 + Location
# @name createPost
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "Written from REST Client", "content": "Some **Markdown**.\n\n- one\n- two" }

### 4. My posts, drafts included -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/posts

### 5. My draft, read by me -> 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}

### 6. Invalid data -> 422 with details
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "", "content": 5 }

### 7. PATCH with no known field -> 422
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{}

### 8. Edit the title only (PATCH keeps the rest) -> 200
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "Written from REST Client, edited" }

### 9. Publish -> 200, publishedAt set by the server
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "published": true }

### 10. Publish again -> 200, publishedAt does NOT change
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "published": true }

### 11. Unpublish -> 200, publishedAt back to null
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "published": false }

### 12. Log in as author2 (replaces the cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author2", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 13. author2 reads author1's draft -> 404 (its existence is a secret)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}

### 14. author2 edits author1's post -> 404
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "Not mine" }

### 15. author2 deletes author1's post -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

### 16. Log in as reader1
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "reader1", "password": "{{$dotenv READER_PASSWORD}}" }

### 17. A reader creates a post -> 403
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/posts
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "title": "Readers cannot write", "content": "Nope" }

### 18. A reader asks for /me/posts -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/me/posts

### 19. Log in as author1 again
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

{ "username": "author1", "password": "{{$dotenv AUTHOR_PASSWORD}}" }

### 20. Delete my post -> 204 (its comments go too, by Cascade)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}
Origin: {{origin}}
X-Requested-With: blog-client

### 21. The deleted post -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/{{createPost.response.body.$.post.id}}

### 22. Non-numeric id -> 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/posts/abc
